steps.instructions:
Goal: the new set in the game, and the portrait's own plate and frame fixed so the art reads.
0. Read the P3 result, §7.12 and §7.14. BEFORE shots with the current art into /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-Raivon/6fa81df3-3b92-5348-855c-cb135734d3b5/scratchpad/portraits/impl/P4_export_ingame/before/ — every screen in §7.14's «Снимки игры» list (commanders album at DL2/4/6/8, commander card at DL4 and Bram at DL2, locked Rai, army tab fan and chips, picker, calendar and calendar:pick, inbox, ftue:1 advisor, ultimatum, peace_offer, expansion, ally_ask, dip2, swap_ai, separate, default HUD and --dl=8, profile, shop, royal reveal, pass).
1. portrait_assets.py: every one of the 150 ids goes through the kit (remove the old builder path); the docstring's three regeneration commands produce exactly the shipped set (commanders 512×588; leaders and ruler rendered at 512 and downscaled to 256×294, premultiplied Lanczos). Render the full set into /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-Raivon/6fa81df3-3b92-5348-855c-cb135734d3b5/scratchpad/portraits/impl/P4_export_ingame/final/ (≈ 2–2.5 h on 4 cores; one id per process in the background; resume-safe).
2. Full strict QA on that folder: every P-A gate of §7.14 (qa_silhouette, qa_framing, qa_contrast, qa_moods with --strict; portrait_qa.py --strict with sidecars; kit --contacts and --stats). Fix and re-render failing ids until all pass; anything you cannot pass is listed with numbers.
3. Copy the 150 PNGs into game/assets/ui/portraits (same names; folder ≤ 40 MB). In the 96 cmd_*.png.import files set mipmaps/generate=true (keep uid and dest paths); leave the leader and ruler imports as they are. Import under the lock.
4. game/scripts/cmd_portrait.gd (re-read first; keep the API: era, era_of, _render, LOOK, RARITY, plate, mood, frame, locked, frame_r, frame_w):
   - plate B (§7.4): vertical gradient rc.lightened(0.18) at the top → rc at the bottom (locked keeps its muted look);
   - the head halo without the dark outline: soft concentric white circles (≈ +12 L* in total), no _fill outline;
   - locked = a flat silhouette from the texture's alpha in INK α 0.3 with no inner detail (e.g. a tiny canvas_item shader on a child node that outputs a constant colour × texture alpha; the plate and frame keep drawing as now);
   - texture_filter = CanvasItem.TEXTURE_FILTER_LINEAR_WITH_MIPMAPS on the portrait node (also inside the KitStill bake: check that baked slots — army chip, album tile — show the new look and no stale bake);
   - LOOK fallback colours synced with the §7.6 palettes;
   - framing fixes only if the shots show a crop problem the art cannot solve.
   Check with --check-only.
5. AFTER shots of the same list; compare pair by pair with BEFORE and judge each against §7: faces and moods readable (the seal at 77 px shows the mood), no clipped hats, crowns or buns, no fishbowl ring, bodies separate from the plates, locked silhouettes flat, eras correct at DL2/4/6/8, the ruler's crown in every era.
6. Direct texture users you may not edit (shop_ui.gd reveal, game_ui.gd pass reward and coach advisor, main.gd chapter reward, hud.gd ruler, game_ui.gd diplomacy card): shoot them; where the 512 commander art aliases at 87–160 px, or the diplomacy name covers the mouth, write the follow-up precisely (file, function, line, the one-line change) — do not edit those files.
7. Tests (test_flow PASS count unchanged, test_commanders, test_cases, test_calendar, test_pass), ui_lint --strict, check_strings.
